    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only `membershipPoints` field (integer, min 0) and updated `membershipLevel` (now 1\u20134) to describe it as derived from points. DTOs are generated from this spec, so this makes `getMembershipPoints()`/`setMembershipPoints()` available on `OwnerDto`.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n- Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints`.\n- New `membershipPoints(owner)` method: starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` `householdSize >= 3`, `+3` tenure over 365 days (registrationDate \u2192 today).\n- Rewrote `membershipLevel(owner)` to map points \u2192 level: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\nBoth fields are returned. The controller's audit log call to `membershipLevel(owner)` still works unchanged.\n\nThe acceptance test (`membershipPoints` = 3, `membershipLevel` = 2 for a fresh owner with email and no namesake \u2014 2+1 = 3 points \u2192 level 2) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
