    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners` (`addOwner`), from the framework layer through the controller body.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Framework, before the method body\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (declared constraints on the DTO):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)`, `@Email` (only if present)\n   - `postcode`, `sharesHousehold`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 no constraints (optional)\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Controller body (`addOwner`, in execution order)\n\n3. **`validateRequiredOwnerFields`** \u2014 rejects blank (present-but-empty) values for `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (checked against its *normalized* form), `city`, `telephone` \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400). This catches whitespace-only values that bean validation lets through.\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner` (`id` and `pets` ignored). *(side-effect: object construction)*\n5. **Normalize telephone** (`normalizeTelephone`) \u2192 strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; **validates** result is `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, then **`validateNationalNumberLength`** (`+61`\u21d29 national digits, `+1`\u21d210). Failure \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400). *Side-effect:* `owner.telephone` set to E.164 form.\n6. **Normalize email** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2192 `null` allowed; else **validates** against `EMAIL_PATTERN`, lower-cases, and **rejects disposable domains** (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400). *Side-effect:* `owner.email` set to trimmed/lower-cased value.\n7. **Normalize address** (`normalizeAddress`) \u2192 strip, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. *Side-effect:* `owner.address` set.\n8. **Validate postcode** (`validatePostcode`) \u2192 `null` allowed; else must be 4 digits and, for a known city (Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane), within its region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n9. **Reject future registration date** (`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`) \u2014 if the *supplied* date is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Runs on the raw date, before roll-forward.\n10. **Default registration date** \u2014 if `null`, set to `LocalDate.now()`. *(side-effect)*\n11. **Roll to business day** (`rollToBusinessDay`) \u2014 Saturday \u2192 +2, Sunday \u2192 +1. *Side-effect:* `owner.registrationDate` set to the adjusted (weekday) date; all later date-derived values use this.\n12. **Reject daily limit** (`rejectDailyLimitReached`) \u2014 if \u2265 100 (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) existing owners share this registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n13. **Reject city at capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 if \u2265 50 (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) existing owners in the same (normalized) city \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`.\n14. **Read `sharesHousehold`** flag (`Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`).\n15. **Assign household id** \u2014 `owner.householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName|postcode`. *(side-effect)*\n16. **Reject duplicate identity** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, if any existing owner has the same `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n17. **Assign possible-duplicate flags** (`assignPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` (earliest existing owner with same last name + postcode but different phone; skipped/cleared when `sharesHousehold`).\n18. **Set namesake count** (`countNamesakes`) \u2014 *side-effect:* count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), snapshotted.\n19. **Set bulk-signup warning** (`isBulkSignupDay`) \u2014 *side-effect:* `true` if > 80 (`BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD`) owners already share the registration date.\n20. **Set household size** (`countHousehold`) \u2014 *side-effect:* existing members with same `householdId` + 1 (1 if `householdId` is null).\n21. **Set customer code** (`buildCustomerCode`) \u2014 *side-effect:* `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode/city, hash = first 8 hex of SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n22. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`, which assigns the `id`. *(primary side-effect)*\n23. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` emits id, customer code, registration date, and computed membership level. *(side-effect)*\n24. **Build response** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived read-only fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber/points/level, locality, contactPreference, telephoneDisplay, identityKey, checkDigit, ageBand); set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`; return **201 Created**. *(side-effects: response headers/body)*\n\nA couple of things worth flagging:\n- `normalizeAddress` is effectively run **twice** \u2014 once inside step 3 (to test blankness of the raw address) and again in step 7 to set the stored value.\n- Many checks (steps 12, 13, 16, 17, 18, 20) each independently call `clinicService.findAllOwners()`, so creation scans the full owner population multiple times.\n- The ordering matters: e.g. the future-date check (9) uses the pre-roll date, while the daily-limit (12) and bulk-warning (19) use the post-roll date."
